#!/usr/bin/env bun
// Fire a test notification through Steam's own toast pipeline, and drive the
// plugin's dev diagnostics. Every command writes a file the plugin's dev poll
// consumes within ~3s, gated on the devFire developer toggle.
//
// Client toasts (Steam's own NotificationStore Test* methods; args are JSON --
// bare numbers and null pass through, quote strings):
//   tools/fire TestDownloadComplete 1073390
//   tools/fire TestFriendOnline
//   tools/fire TestFriendMessage null '"Ready to play?"'
//   tools/fire TestAchievement 570
//   NEVER TestIncomingVoiceChat: the fake call cannot resolve and wedges
//   Steam's toast queue until restart (AGENTS.md).
//
// Server-sourced (eSource=2) types, whose shipped test methods are stubbed, go
// through the real ingestion path instead (OnServerNotification):
//   tools/fire --wishlist [appid]              store-bound wishlist toast
//                                              (defaults to 1073390, Aircar)
//   tools/fire --server <type> '<body-json>'   any type; see the body_data
//                                              fields in docs/steam-routing.md
//
// Diagnostics (results land in the plugin log):
//   tools/fire --overlay-info                dump overlay browser PIDs
//   tools/fire --replay inspect              dump the stashed handler entries
//   tools/fire --replay invoke [toast-name]  invoke a stashed handler
//
// Runs under bun on every platform (on Windows: bun tools/fire ...). The
// runtime directory and the .star location follow backend/main.lua
// (tools/lib/snn.ts).
import { main } from './lib/cli/fire';

await main(import.meta.path);
